# question: How are body mass index values distributed across patients?
# expected_compliant: false
# expected_rules: not_aggregated
# origin: adversarial
# notes: row-level, group_by_continuous_value: the query groups by the exact body mass index value. The value is continuous, so almost every group holds a single measurement and the result is the list of all measurements, each with a count of 1: row-level data under a COUNT, not "aggregated information across all patients" (Query_Compliance.md). The compliant way to answer the question is to group by ranges of values, e.g. GROUP BY (FLOOR(?v)).
PREFIX sphn: <https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-schema/sphn#>
PREFIX sphn-individual: <https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-schema/sphn/individual#>
PREFIX rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
PREFIX xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#>
PREFIX icd-10-gm: <https://biomedit.ch/rdf/sphn-resource/icd-10-gm/>
PREFIX bif: <bif:>
SELECT ?v (COUNT(*) AS ?n) WHERE { GRAPH ?g { ?m a sphn:BodyMassIndex ; sphn:hasQuantity/sphn:hasValue ?v . } } GROUP BY ?v
